{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception as a single automaton, with states representing sensor situations and action-commitment. The specification enforces conservative exploration: random_walk is used in clear, move_forward is only used in a dedicated commit state, and any obstacle event forces a one-shot turn recovery before returning to exploration. Only one controllable is enabled per state, and all uncontrollables are total. No forward or random_walk is allowed in obstacle states. Recovery from obs_left uses rotate_clockwise; from obs_right uses rotate_counterclockwise; from obs_front uses rotate_clockwise. Full_rotate is only allowed in a deliberate scan state, not as immediate recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Merge motion and perception into a single plant automaton for clarity and to match the event semantics.",
    "Specification enforces safe, conservative exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward only in forward_commit, and immediate turn recovery on obstacles, with deterministic transitions and no unsafe oscillations."
  ],
